    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d478">

                <pb facs="0555" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1927v03/pg453"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.00/5214: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Summerlin</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-12-31T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                                1927—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>44. Referring to telegram December 31, 10 a.m., from Managua.<anchor n="50"
                        xml:id="d478-f1"/> Department is deeply concerned over the situation in
                    Nicaragua. All evidence received both from Munro and from American armed forces
                    tends to prove that bandits in Nueva Segovia are receiving material assistance
                    from Honduras. Department expects you to impress upon President Paz necessity
                    for preventing this. Keep the Department informed by telegraph of whatever
                    measures are taken as result of your representations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d478-f1" n="50" xml:id="d478-f1-content">
                <p>See undated telegram No. 391 from the Chargé in Nicaragua, <hi
